WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:17.563
"Mowgli is probably okay, Baloo," Bagheera said.

2
00:00:17.564 --> 00:00:20.440
"He's smart and you've taught him well."

3
00:00:20.441 --> 00:00:24.357
Bagheera licked a paw thoughtfully.

4
00:00:24.358 --> 00:00:28.860
"But we do need a plan to get him back."

5
00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:32.043
"Well, that's a problem," Baloo said.

6
00:00:32.044 --> 00:00:38.176
"Because those monkeys aren't scared of either one of us. Hey!"

7
00:00:38.177 --> 00:00:40.611
He sat up with a jerk.

8
00:00:40.612 --> 00:00:46.649
"The monkeys are afraid of Kaa. Let's go talk to him!"

9
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.910
"I don't really like talking to the python.

10
00:00:49.911 --> 00:00:55.941
I'm not sure he's our friend. And . . ." Bagheera shuddered.

11
00:00:55.942 --> 00:00:59.430
"He has spooky eyes."

12
00:00:59.431 --> 00:01:02.952
"Come on, Bagheera. Kaa is very cunning.

13
00:01:02.953 --> 00:01:05.523
Let's go see if he can help us."

14
00:01:05.524 --> 00:01:11.672
Bagheera sighed. "Fine."

15
00:01:11.673 --> 00:01:15.943
Kaa lay on a warm rock in the afternoon sun.

16
00:01:15.944 --> 00:01:20.327
His long body was twisted into coils and curves.

17
00:01:20.328 --> 00:01:26.444
He was admiring his new brown and yellow skin.

18
00:01:26.445 --> 00:01:32.586
"Be careful, Bagheera," Baloo whispered as they approached.

19
00:01:32.587 --> 00:01:37.405
"Kaa is always a little blind after he has changed his skin.

20
00:01:37.406 --> 00:01:40.439
This makes him quick to strike."

21
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:47.787
Kaa was not a poisonous snake, but he was still very dangerous.

22
00:01:47.788 --> 00:01:53.090
He could coil tightly around someone in a deadly squeeze.

23
00:01:53.091 --> 00:01:58.168
"Good day, Kaa!" Baloo called.

24
00:01:58.169 --> 00:02:07.098
"Oh, Baloo, what are you doing here?"

25
00:02:07.099 --> 00:02:11.205
"We came to ask for your help," the bear replied.

26
00:02:11.206 --> 00:02:16.078
"We need to find the monkeys. It's a bit of an emergency."

27
00:02:16.079 --> 00:02:21.449
"Sss." Kaa let out a lazy hiss.

28
00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:28.907
"I'm tired and full. I'm in no mood to chase monkeys right now."

29
00:02:28.908 --> 00:02:31.820
Baloo flashed a look at Bagheera.

30
00:02:31.821 --> 00:02:35.289
What if Kaa wouldn't help them?

31
00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:39.670
"Um, Kaa . . ." Bagheera swallowed.

32
00:02:39.671 --> 00:02:46.212
"Did you know that the monkeys call you a footless yellow earthworm?"

33
00:02:46.213 --> 00:02:49.269
Kaa's eyes flashed with anger.

34
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.738
"They call me an earthworm?"

35
00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:56.879
"Something like that," Bagheera replied.

36
00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.568
"And sometimes they make fun of you," Baloo chimed in.

37
00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:08.386
"They say you have no teeth. And you're afraid of goats' horns."

38
00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:13.381
"What?" Kaa coiled up tightly.

39
00:03:13.382 --> 00:03:18.469
The big swallowing muscles on his throat rippled and bulged.

40
00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:22.378
"Why are you looking for the monkeys?"

41
00:03:22.379 --> 00:03:27.616
"Well, as you know, I am the man cub's teacher," Baloo began.

42
00:03:27.625 --> 00:03:31.596
"He usually listens to me, but once, he—"

43
00:03:31.597 --> 00:03:33.909
Bagheera was getting impatient.

44
00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:38.739
They didn't have time for long stories.

45
00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:42.348
"The trouble is this, Kaa," he said, jumping in.

46
00:03:42.349 --> 00:03:46.762
"Those silly nut-stealers have stolen away the man cub."

47
00:03:46.763 --> 00:03:50.548
"He's a wonderful man cub," Baloo said.

48
00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:55.941
"Mowgli is the smartest and boldest of all the man cubs in the world.

49
00:03:55.942 --> 00:04:00.724
I—we—love him, Kaa."

50
00:04:00.725 --> 00:04:05.773
"Ssss!" Kaa wove his head back and forth.

51
00:04:05.774 --> 00:04:13.281
"The man cub belongs with you—not those monkeys. You are his family."

52
00:04:13.282 --> 00:04:15.940
"That's why we're here," Bagheera said.

53
00:04:15.941 --> 00:04:21.325
"The monkeys are afraid of only one animal in the jungle—you."

54
00:04:21.326 --> 00:04:28.423
"So we're hoping you'll help us find them," Baloo added. "Please."

55
00:04:28.424 --> 00:04:34.541
"Those horrible monkeys chatter constantly," Kaa muttered.

56
00:04:34.542 --> 00:04:38.230
"And they are foolish and lazy."

57
00:04:38.231 --> 00:04:40.844
He swung toward Bagheera.

58
00:04:40.845 --> 00:04:45.224
"What do the monkeys call me—a yellow fish?"

59
00:04:45.225 --> 00:04:47.614
Bagheera lowered his head.

60
00:04:47.615 --> 00:04:53.468
"A yellow earthworm. And other terrible names."

61
00:04:53.469 --> 00:04:59.519
"I'm going to remind them to speak well of me!" Kaa snapped.

62
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.316
"Where did they go?"

63
00:05:02.317 --> 00:05:06.330
"We thought you might know, Kaa," Baloo said.

64
00:05:06.331 --> 00:05:13.045
"I do know they moved to a different part of the jungle today." Kaa hissed.

65
00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:18.861
"I heard them laughing among the treetops earlier. But I—"

66
00:05:18.862 --> 00:05:23.517
"Up! Up!" A sharp cry came from above.

67
00:05:23.518 --> 00:05:29.347
Baloo looked up. Rann was flying across the sky.

68
00:05:29.348 --> 00:05:33.111
"I have a message from Mowgli!" the hawk cried.

69
00:05:33.112 --> 00:05:36.323
"The monkeys have carried him deep into the jungle.

70
00:05:36.324 --> 00:05:43.089
He is now beyond the river—in Monkey City!"
